# `{ a, ...(p !== undefined ? { p } : undefined) }`: the front end lays the spread on each way: the one defines `p`, the other copies `undefined`. undefined, null, a boolean, a number, a bigint and a symbol have no properties of their own
# to copy: nothing is built for such a copy, so nothing is taken to have written the literal, and the read of `a` behind the meeting is answered by what the literal was made with. A text has its characters: it is copied.
# f1 = pick, f2 = keep, f3 = text
